# Editorial routing

Never put articles in `carlosrabelo/` (GitHub profile README only).

Override if the user says "só no .br" or "nos dois".

## Campus engineering → both sites (not a literal translation)

VLAN, inventory, SUAP, switches, machine fleet, public-IT operations tooling.

- Same English slug.
- `carlosrabelo.com/content/projects/{slug}.md` — short English showcase.
- `carlosrabelo.com.br/content/engenharia/{slug}.md` — Portuguese with institutional context.
- Cross-link both pages at the end.

## One site

**`carlosrabelo.com`** (English, international portfolio)

- Shipable tool/repo → `content/projects/{slug}.md`
- Engineering/learning article → `content/articles/{slug}.md`
- Bio → `content/about.md`
- Do not copy gobi, bip38, learning-go, act, or GRC to `.br`.

**`carlosrabelo.com.br`** (Portuguese hub)

- Campus-applied engineering only (Negev, TatuScan pattern) → `content/engenharia/{slug}.md`
- Coordination, governance, distro, CMS → `content/gestao/{slug}.md`
- Focus, career, behavior → `content/ensaios/{slug}.md`
- Bio → `content/sobre/index.md`

## Frontmatter

English filenames. Set `section` and `categories` to the directory name. Tags: short, unaccented, language of the site. Keep aliases for old `/posts/` and `/codes/` URLs when moving or replacing a page.
